From 8fd1bca50bed9d99109aa36e53dc640898bbe89e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Baierl <ichgeh@imkreisrum.de>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:54:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: amlogic: amvdec: h264: abort a frame if no capture
 is picked

If no CAPTURE buffer can be picked for a new picture, the threaded
interrupt handler aborts only for field pictures. For frame pictures it
returns without an action for the firmware, so the job never finishes.

Abort for frame pictures too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
index 7a82fa5..cb924bd 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
@@ -1822,8 +1822,7 @@ static irqreturn_t codec_h264_threaded_isr(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 			codec_h264_multi_inject_sps_rpm(sess);
 			if (!h264->multi_pic_started) {
 				if (codec_h264_multi_pick_capture(sess)) {
-					if (h264->multi_field_picture)
-						codec_h264_multi_abort(sess);
+					codec_h264_multi_abort(sess);
 					return IRQ_HANDLED;
 				}
 				if (codec_h264_multi_config_decode_buf(sess)) {
-- 
2.43.0

